  "executive_briefing": "The global corporate and international tax landscape in 2026 continues to experience deep structural shifts driven by the ongoing institutionalization of the OECD Pillar Two 15% global minimum tax. Governments, particularly within hubs like Singapore and the broader ASEAN-6 block, are proactively fine-tuning corporate tax rates, incentives, and rebates to preserve foreign direct investment competitiveness. Concurrently, tax administrations are ramping up digital compliance requirements through phased mandates for e-invoicing and real-time transaction controls. On the trade front, persistent geopolitical friction and unilateral tariff adjustments by major economies maintain high volatility and acute market awareness.",
